==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₃reǵ-}}
Borrowed from {{bor|en|NL.|rectum}}, clipping of {{der|en|la|[[rectum]] [[intestinum]]|lit=the straight intestine}}, {{m|la|rectum}}, neuter of {{m|la|rectus||straight}}. See {{m|en|right}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɹɛktəm/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-I learned some phrases-rectum.wav|Audio (UK)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛktəm|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|recta|s}}

# {{lb|en|anatomy}} The [[terminal]] part of the large [[intestine]] through which [[feces]] pass after [[exit]]ing the [[colon]], but before leaving the body through the [[anus]].

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|rectal}}

